{"id":"setenforce.8","n":"setenforce","s":"8","src":{"r":{"pkg":"libselinux-utils","ver":"3.6-3.el9","repo":"BaseOS","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/BaseOS/x86_64/os/Packages/l/libselinux-utils-3.6-3.el9.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/setenforce.8.gz","sha256":"0903fc2340c50a16178e8260dd6fe1f48578cf604088eb91f8aa591b441b1127","date":"7 April 2004","origin":"dwalsh@redhat.com"},"u":{"pkg":"selinux-utils","ver":"3.3-1build2","repo":"jammy/universe","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/universe/libs/libselinux/selinux-utils_3.3-1build2_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/setenforce.8.gz","sha256":"3448dd1d7a76343e384c627cbf9c05b410b276953c3ad60110774f40b7ccc734","date":"7 April 2004","origin":"dwalsh@redhat.com"}},"nopt":{"r":0,"u":0},"desc":"modify the mode SELinux is running in","same":true,"doc":[["NAME","<p>setenforce - modify the mode SELinux is running in</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>setenforce</b> [<b>Enforcing</b>|<b>Permissive</b>|<b>1</b>|<b>0</b>]</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>Use <b>Enforcing</b> or <b>1</b> to put SELinux in enforcing mode. <br> Use <b>Permissive</b> or <b>0</b> to put SELinux in permissive mode.</p> <p>If SELinux is disabled and you want to enable it, or SELinux is enabled and you want to disable it, please see <b>selinux</b>(8).</p>"],["AUTHOR","<p>Dan Walsh, &lt;dwalsh@redhat.com&gt;</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>selinux</b>(8), <b>getenforce</b>(8), <b>selinuxenabled</b>(8)</p>"]]}